course: dictionary
lesson: 13392
title: Heaves: lifting, rising and sighing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heaves is an action word, a verb. It has several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one to use. Ask yourself: is someone lifting something, is something rising and falling, or is someone letting out a sigh?
explain: «Dad heaves the wet sofa up the stairs.» Heaves means lifts with great effort. The clues are wet sofa and stairs: nobody lifts a heavy sofa easily.
explain: «The boat rocks as the sea heaves.» Here heaves means rises and falls strongly, like waves. «She heaves a sigh of relief» means she lets out a big, deep sigh. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: In tug-of-war, the teacher shouts «Heave!» for one big pull. Sailors shout «Heave ho!» when they all pull together. Both use heave to mean a strong, joint effort.
fact: Heaves is a form of the verb heave: heave, heaves, heaved, heaving.
fact: «Heaves» means lifts, pulls or throws something heavy with great effort.
fact: «Heaves» can mean rises and falls strongly, like the sea or someone's chest when breathing hard.
fact: «Heaves a sigh» means lets out a big, deep sigh.
fact: The informal noun «the heaves» means retching, which is trying to be sick.
exercise: «Dad heaves the wet sofa up the stairs.» What does heaves mean? | Whispers softly | Relaxes on | Paints | *Lifts with great effort
exercise: «The boat rocks as the sea heaves.» What does heaves mean here? | Freezes solid | *Rises and falls strongly | Makes a loud bang | Stays perfectly still
exercise: «After the race, Sam heaves a big sigh.» What does heaves a sigh mean? | *Lets out a big, deep sigh | Takes a quick nap | Shouts for help | Laughs at a joke
test: What does heave mean in «The team gives one last heave in tug-of-war»? | *A big pull with great effort | A gentle wave | A loud song | A quiet whisper
test: What does heaves mean in «Her chest heaves after the run»? | Stops moving completely | Turns bright red | Falls asleep | *Rises and falls quickly as she breathes hard
exam: Which clue in «He heaves the heavy sack onto his back» tells you heaves means lifts with effort? | back | *heavy sack | onto | sack and back are the same
